**The outcome.** If any check fails (a mechanical exit, Check 2 not `0`, the scan without exit 0
or its summary line, a high finding, a Check 6 failure) or the drift result is not `clean`, it
writes no record: name the gate that did not pass and say review runs next. Nothing is retried
and nothing is deleted here. If
`{{ WTR }}/{{ config.work_docs.dir }}REVIEW-{slug}-{date}.md` already holds a real review (no
`review_kind: light-check`), it writes no record either — never overwrite a real review — and
review runs next.

Otherwise every gate passed and the drift is `result: clean`:
Write `{{ WTR }}/{{ config.work_docs.dir }}REVIEW-{slug}-{date}.md` (review's own file name) with
this frontmatter — the drift block is the one from gate 5 — and a one-line body naming the gates
(after Check 2's `"gate_source": "spec"`, `regression: pytest from SPEC (no CI file)`):

```yaml
---
type: review
review_kind: light-check
task_slug: {slug}
status: PASSED
created: {YYYY-MM-DD}
verification_key: <the key printed after Check 2>
drift_verdict:
  result: clean
  scope_violations: []
  scenario_misses: []
  task_slug: {slug}
  computed_at: <the output of date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ>
checks:
  mechanical: pass | n-a
  regression: pass
  security: pass
  spec_requirement: pass | warn | n-a
  structural: not-run
---
```

Take `computed_at` from `date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ` as you write the record. A date alone, or a
time without its zone, reads as no record.

`status: PASSED` is not `APPROVED`: nothing graded the change. Under autopilot, execute's boundary
then passes over review and verify only when this record is the newest REVIEW for the slug, was
computed after the session armed, carries the tree's current `verification_key` and passing
`checks`, and Check 2's own `run` marker for that key is fresh; otherwise review runs next. A
typed `/hm:review` or `/hm:verify` still runs in full.
